    "gatheredBy": "load-sport-data, the 2025-26 UEFA Champions League knockout phase as played, from the knockout play-offs to the final. A two-legged tie is one match: its scores are the aggregate after both legs (extra time included), it is scheduled at the first leg's kickoff, and its home side hosted the first leg. No tie was level on aggregate. The league phase's top eight go straight into the Round of 16, named on the away side of their tie; the play-off winners fill the home side. The final, in Budapest, is the one neutral-site match, level after extra time and won on penalties, with its half-time score from the goal minutes; a tie has no half-time score. Kickoffs are the page's CET (to 28 March) and CEST times. Seeds and rankings are the league phase places. ESPN's scoreboards agree on the play-off first legs of 17 February and on the final's shoot-out. Odds to win are made up by seed.",
